# Lost and found in Russian: исчезла, нашлась, оказалось
subtitle: "The medal disappears from the wall at «Нева» and turns up again: lost, found, disappeared, turned up and it turned out that, in Russian."
tags: ["russian","потерять найти","оказаться","russian verbs","russian grammar"]
teaches: ["grammar/aspect","vocabulary/work"]
thumb: "band \"Where did the medal go?\""
voices: {"a":"gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would","b":"gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated"}
next: {"title":"Instead of taking the tram in Russian: вместо того чтобы…","href":"https://www.drawcast.app/#gh=hmelberg/drawcast-library/russian-from-zero/186-russian-instead-of.cast"}

